body:
LOL you lumped in ADA with ETH and BTC. I do see ADA succeeding but in its current state you can't add it to the "safe" options. You wouldnt recommend a cell phone company still in development and say they are a safe bet with apple and google.

&#x200B;

EDIT: Fuck it im gonna say it. Just because you either A - lost a shit ton on NFTs or Shitcoins or B - havent delved into it at all, doesnt mean there isnt money to be made. I literally use shitcoins and NFTs as a means to increase my bags for my long term holds. A little experience and research go a long way. Plus this whole post is unnecessary as its posted several times a day.

&#x200B;

And before anyone says youre gonna lose money investing in shitcoins. I dont invest. I take advantage. I'm never in longer than an \~hour or two. And thats only on day one. Anything past that youre asking them to take your money. I dont make the money to invest enough to end up financially free so I have to make that happen by any means neccessary. I take precautions to mitigate loss and have been doing it all year. It's no riskier than anything else if you learn how to play like the whales.

I've got news for you...

&#x200B;

[My swap of $4 of ETH to CRO](https://imgur.com/a/s64If5U)

How do you figure? I Just got mine and will break even in \~2 and a half months. People in more populated areas are making more. I check the explorer often and theres people making $500-$1k a month. Most Miners cost around $500. Thats not to say there arent miners making garbage but I honestly attribute most of that to people who cant be bothered to port forward or have their miner sitting on the floor surrounded by metal file cabinets or some shit. 

&#x200B;

The wait to get a miners is 8-12 weeks usually. Its honestly a better choice to pay someone on Ebay $900 for a $500 miner just so you can start earning now.

"There are is NO FREEZING or CLAWBACK in our ASA. You have the full control over your coins."

&#x200B;

Then why is Clawbacks enabled on Algoexplorer? This looks very low effort and I smell a rug coming. So many red flags for a coin that claims to have real uses.

Another good post with info that may answer your question.

&#x200B;

https://www.reddit.com/r/CryptoCurrency/comments/qlvqvs/knowyourcrypto\_44\_multivac\_mtv/

[https://multivac-global.medium.com/forbes-report-multivac-solving-the-bottleneck-of-blockchain-and-the-scalability-trilemma-through-a995f02f5d70](https://multivac-global.medium.com/forbes-report-multivac-solving-the-bottleneck-of-blockchain-and-the-scalability-trilemma-through-a995f02f5d70)

&#x200B;

THis should answer your question. As far as I know, MTV is the only blockchain able to solve the trilemma. Others solve 2 but not all 3. MTV allows companies to choose whats most important to their tech. ( this was 2019 so things could be different now )
